      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1161515658,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I think this is a better pattern:\n```\nif (!wmem_strbuf_utf8_validate(...)) {\n    wmem_strbuf_make_valid(...);\n}\n```\nIt's better because it is a lot cheaper for the most common case of valid UTF-8. We can of course wrap it in a new method for `wmem_strbuf_t` (wmem_strbuf_sanitize?). The reason these need to be separate is to allow inserting a ws_log call in the middle.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
