        {
          "id": 1161536017,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Yes you're right, considering the probabilites, better to validate twice on a bad string in the course in sanitizing than to do the overhead of sanitizing.\n\nShould there be a way to call `wmem_strbuf_utf8_validate` with a null pointer when we don't care about the  value of endptr? I believe right now it will crash.",
